```

| Runtime | Typical CLI / UI | Example ids |
|---------|------------------|-------------|
| `cursor` | Cursor Task `model=` | `composer-2.5-fast`, `gpt-5-mini`, … |
| `codex` | `codex -m …` / `config.toml` | `gpt-5.5`, `gpt-5.4-mini`, `gpt-5.3-codex` |
| `claude` | Claude Code model picker | per your account |

Reserved in any block: `auto` (UI-only, not passed to tools).

## Orchestrator delegation

```bash
node .ai/runtime/orchestrator-state.mjs active-runtime
node .ai/runtime/orchestrator-state.mjs model-hint --role review
```

- **Do not** pass `--runtime cursor` when you are in Codex (or the reverse).
- Override detection: `AIFORGE_ACTIVE_RUNTIME=codex` (or `cursor`, `claude`).
- Follow JSON `instruction` — Cursor uses Task `model=`; Codex uses `codex -m`; they are **not** interchangeable.

## Editing

Change tiers in `agents.modelTiers`. Add slugs under `agents.runtimeModels.<runtime>.<tier>`. Re-run `sync` to refresh `.ai/project.model-profiles.json`.

`saveConfig` / `loadConfig` rejects obvious cross-runtime slug mistakes (e.g. `gpt-5.5-medium` under `codex`).
